Package: BioExplainR
Type: Package
Title: Evidence-Constrained Explanation and Error Diagnosis for Bioinformatics R Objects
Version: 0.4.0.9000
Authors@R: person(given = "BioExplainR", family = "contributors", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "maintainer@example.org")
Author: BioExplainR contributors
Maintainer: BioExplainR contributors <maintainer@example.org>
Description: A beginner-oriented framework that converts common bioinformatics
    R results (differential expression tables, 'DESeq2' results, 'clusterProfiler'
    enrichment results, 'Seurat'/'SingleCellExperiment' objects, 'ggplot2' plots)
    into a compact, inspectable intermediate context. Statistical facts are
    computed deterministically in R; an optional large language model (OpenAI-
    compatible or Anthropic Messages protocol, user-supplied URL/key/model) only
    organises language. It also records R execution with warnings, errors and
    call stacks, offers offline error categories, validates user-supplied fixes
    in a separate R process against explicit invariants, and writes Markdown or
    HTML reports without secrets or raw expression matrices. Retrieves traceable
    database and literature evidence, validates explicit model claims, checks
    plots against source results, integrates dependent analyses into projects,
    and provides interpretation benchmarks and educational assessment tools. It
    also includes an optional local Shiny browser workbench for model settings,
    R runtime inspection, recorded code execution, natural-language analysis,
    and common bioinformatics plots.
